KRDC gets a per-host RDP option, "Remote pointer: painted into the video
by the server" (embeddedCursor in the host's group of krdcrc, Bool,
default false). On, the client advertises no pointer cache in its
capabilities (both pointer cache sizes 0), which tells the server this
client draws no pointer shapes; a server that can, such as KRdp with
this repository's krdp-embed-cursor.patch, then paints its own pointer
into the video and sends the null pointer, so the picture shows where
the remote mouse is, as the remote screen does, for a viewer that only
watches. Stock KRdp 6.8 crashes on a client without a pointer cache (it
means to refuse one, but checks before the client's capabilities arrive
and then evicts from an empty cache), and other servers are untested;
the tooltip warns that a server without support may fail. Off, nothing
changes: the sizes stay at FreeRDP's defaults and the server sends
shapes as before. View > Show Local Cursor is left alone: with it on,
the viewer's own pointer shows over the remote one, which some want.
Made against krdc 26.08.2.

diff --color -ruN --no-dereference a/core/krdc.kcfg b/core/krdc.kcfg
